# No Build Requests

Never run build commands or ask for permissions to build unless the user explicitly requests a build.

## Do not run

- `xcodebuild`, XcodeBuildMCP build tools, or simulator build-and-run
- `swift build`, `npm run build`, `yarn build`, `pnpm build`, `make`, Gradle, Maven, Cargo build, etc.
- Any command whose primary purpose is compiling or linking the app

## Do not request elevated permissions

- Do not request `all`, `full_network`, or other permissions solely to run a build or resolve package dependencies for verification.

## Instead

- Rely on static checks (linters, type errors in the editor) when verifying changes.
- Tell the user what to run locally if a build is the only way to confirm something—and only when they ask or when a build is truly required to complete their request.

## Exception

- Run a build only when the user explicitly asks (e.g. "build the project", "run xcodebuild", "verify it compiles").
